# The data files under omen/ are intentionally tracked. Do not ignore them — but note
# they are tracked for three different reasons, and the refresh Action treats them
# differently (see .github/workflows/refresh.yml). The site is a Worker + R2, not
# Cloudflare Pages: worker.js serves the R2 copy live and only falls back to the
# committed one on an R2 miss.
#
#   Committed every run — durable history / state that only exists in git:
#     snapshots.csv, china-snapshots.csv, capex-snapshots.csv  (append-only history)
#     alert-state.json  (alert dedup; ephemeral CI would re-alert without it)
#
#   Committed every run — bundled static assets, NOT in R2, so the committed copy is
#   the only copy the site ever serves:
#     china-data.json, china-history.json, app-charts.json
#     (influencers.json and capex-data.json are in R2, but are ~KB, so they are
#      committed every run too and stay a warm fallback)
#
#   Bootstrap seed, refreshed periodically rather than per run:
#     market-data.json — 171 KB rewritten every 30 min and served live from R2, so
#     committing it hourly was pure repo bloat. It stays tracked because the Worker's
#     R2-miss fallback needs a bundled copy at deploy time; the Action re-commits it
#     only when the tracked copy is older than 7 days.
#
# market-data.js is likewise tracked but not in the commit loop at all — a hand-refreshed
# stale seed, the existing precedent for the above.
